Work over an algebraically closed field of characteristic 2. Let X be the generic curve of genus 1 (i.e. a generic elliptic curve over this field). Determine whether there exists a non-constant rational function f : X → P^1 of degree 5 satisfying the following:

(a) the Galois group of the Galois closure of the function field extension k(X)/k(P^1) (the monodromy group of f) is isomorphic to the alternating group A_5;

(b) f has exactly five branch points, and over each branch point the ramification structure of f is described by the partition (3) — equivalently, above each branch point there is a single ramification point of ramification index 3 together with two unramified points (so the inertia data are five 3-cycles, giving ramification type (3, 3, 3, 3, 3)).

